{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>From the beginning.</b> And not every beginning — for not all fruits are obligated in first-fruits, but only the seven species alone. It says here ״אֶרֶץ״ and it says elsewhere (Deuteronomy 8) ״a land of wheat and barley, etc.״ Just as there — the seven species through which the land of Israel is praised, so too here — the praise of the land of Israel, that they are seven species. (Sifrei; Menachot 4)" "<b>Olive of oil.</b> An aguri olive — its oil gathered within it. (Sifrei; Berachot 39)" "<b>And honey.</b> It is date honey. (Sifrei)" "<b>From the beginning.</b> A person goes into his field and sees a fig that has ripened — he ties a reed around it as a sign and says, ״This is first-fruits.״ (Sifrei; Bikkurim 3)"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:25.054249792Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}